i thought I might revisit the engine loop and the cmd / result stuff.

All Commands can have a baseclass which means 'this command is intended for that service'

frontend service: only service to not receive commands, only issues them. only result consumer
    get_request -> the engine can get cmds here
    post_response -> the engine drops off results here

other services: Consumer commands, returning a new command or a result
    they can have a handle_cmd method.
    This will convert a cmd into either a new cmd (as in the case of kb converting a frontent generated kb command to a promptrender cmd), or a result (as when for instance there was no button inhabitant, and kb converts to a 'noinhab' type result)

So the engine can have a method scoped 'item: Result | KBCmd | IngestionCmd | PromptCmd | ExitCmd' variable
prior to loop, it declares 'item = None'
Engine loop pseudo:
````
while not isinstance(item, ExitCmd):
    if item is None: item = frontend.get_request # this will return a cmd eventually
    match item:
        case x() : service_x.handle_cmd
        case y() : service_x.handle_cmd
    if isinstance(item, Result) : frontent.post_response(item)
````

what do you think? 

